# Reversed out: pale ink on a near-black sheet. Read the warning before you print it.
#
# THIS THEME IS A DELIBERATE EXCEPTION to everything else in the library, and to
# DESIGN.md D10's "defaults are chosen for paper, not for a monitor". It is here
# because a dark page genuinely is the right answer on a screen, on an e-ink
# reader, and projected — and because refusing to ship it would only mean
# everyone wrote a worse one.
#
# What it costs on paper, so nobody finds out at the printer:
#
#   * Roughly 90% ink coverage. On a laser printer that is most of a cartridge
#     for a hundred sheets; on inkjet it is worse and slower.
#   * Banding. A large flat fill is the hardest thing for a consumer engine to
#     lay down evenly, and the seams between passes show across an A4 field.
#   * Paper curl and offsetting. That much wet or fused toner buckles 20lb
#     stock and can transfer to the next sheet in the tray.
#   * You cannot write on it. Ballpoint, pencil and most gel pens are all
#     darker than the sheet. It is a display theme.
#
# On screen, though, everything below is chosen the same way the light themes
# are: the ink slots keep their relationships, so a document swapped onto this
# theme still reads as the same document.

# The five semantic slots. Every shipped theme defines all five, so a document
# that writes `color: {ink}` rather than a literal grey survives a theme swap —
# including onto `midnight`, where the ink is pale and the paper is dark.
vars
  paper:  gray(0.14)
  ink:    gray(0.92)
  muted:  gray(0.62)
  rule:   gray(0.4)
  accent: gray(1)


defaults
  # 1. Body ink: not pure white. gray(0.92) takes the glare off a large dark
  # field and stops the type from haloing.
  font: IBM Plex Mono
  font-size: 9pt
  color: gray(0.92)
  line-height: 1.35

  # 2. The writing surface, inverted: rules sit ABOVE the sheet tint instead of
  # below it, and the 0.5pt weight compensates for a thin light line on dark
  # losing more to any renderer's antialiasing than a dark line on white.
  line-color: gray(0.4)
  line-width: 0.5pt
  line-pitch: 6mm
  dot-size: 0.85pt
  grid-major: 5
  grid-major-width: 0.7pt
  margin-rule-color: gray(0.55)

  # 3. Frames.
  border-color: gray(0.45)
  border-style: solid
  border-radius: 2pt

  # 4. Labels.
  title-color: gray(0.72)
  title-size: 6.5pt
  title-weight: bold
  title-style: plain
  title-transform: upper
  title-tracking: 0.8pt

  # 5. The sheet. This is the line that costs the cartridge.
  background: gray(0.14)
